WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:07.754
[Narrator] Introducing live-translated audio, for wireless conference headsets. One speaker. Every language. On the headsets your attendees already wear.

2
00:00:08.104 --> 00:00:13.041
[Narrator] Watch. Channel one carries the speaker, in English. Channel two carries the translation, in French.

3
00:00:13.541 --> 00:00:16.358
[Channel 1, a woman speaking English] Good morning everyone, and welcome to the conference.

4
00:00:17.558 --> 00:00:19.792
[Channel 2, translated in a female voice] Bonjour à tous et bienvenue à la conférence.

5
00:00:20.192 --> 00:00:23.569
[Narrator] A woman is speaking, so the translation is read in a female voice.

6
00:00:24.169 --> 00:00:25.358
[Channel 1, a man speaking English] Thank you, Claire.

7
00:00:26.258 --> 00:00:26.969
[Channel 2, translated in a male voice] Merci, Claire.

8
00:00:27.369 --> 00:00:36.929
[Narrator] Now a man is speaking, so the voice switches to a male one. You choose the gender, the voice and the accent your listeners hear. Or turn on automatic gender detection, for when two people share the stage.

9
00:00:37.729 --> 00:00:42.046
[Narrator] The numbers. The translated voice starts about one second after each sentence ends.

10
00:00:42.346 --> 00:00:48.176
[Narrator] The right voice was chosen ninety-six times out of a hundred, tested on sixty-six real speakers, one at a time.

11
00:00:48.476 --> 00:00:51.303
[Narrator] More than fifty languages, and no internet needed in the hall.

12
00:00:52.003 --> 00:00:57.522
[Narrator] Live-translated audio. Add translated channels to your headset system. conferencecaptioning.com

